; set-filament-diameter
; Records the filament diameter a tool is set up for after a conversion (2.85 <-> 1.75
; mm hotend/extruder parts) - one call to hardware/confirm-filament-diameter.g: a dropdown with
; the configured value preselected, persisted per tool in
; sys/generated/filament-diameter<tool>.g, applied at once with M200 and by config.g
; at every boot. It is the first half of the calibration key (filament-profile/calibration-key.g): the
; e-steps, NLE and PA results and nozzle-<key>.g are filed per filament diameter and
; nozzle, so after a conversion the profiles switch to the files of the new diameter
; and ask for the missing ones. Also used by the spool consumption tracker.
; Cancelling keeps the configured value.
; Not while a job is being processed, paused included: the value changes M200 and the
; consumption maths of the running print.

if job.file.fileName != null
  echo "Error: a print job is running - abort!"
  M99

var tool = min(max(state.currentTool, 0), 1)
M98 P"0:/sys/meltingplot/hardware/confirm-filament-diameter.g" T{var.tool}

M291 R"Filament diameter" P{"Tool " ^ var.tool ^ ": " ^ global.filament_diameter[var.tool] ^ " mm. Calibrations are filed per filament diameter - run the calibration macros e-steps, nle and pressure-advance where results are missing."} S1 T0
M400 ; sbc specific
